From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: local wireless only with a network

Every 1 s (off the frame's path) BananaDS checks for a network to play on: an interface other than loopback that
is up and running (on the handheld, wlan0 connected: BananaOS keeps wlan0's address after a disconnect, not its
RUNNING flag) with an IPv4 address. Without one, Host, Join and Auto stay chosen (bananads.conf isn't touched) but
nothing starts and no join is tried; a session ends when the network goes (the others look again, Auto's re-elect);
when it is back, Host hosts again, Join looks for hosts and Auto starts over once the game's wifi is on. Nintendo
WFC goes through slirp and isn't affected.

The menu: Quick settings' LAN multiplayer row says "No Wi-Fi" in grey and doesn't open; an open page turns its
Mode, Players and Hosts rows off and says to connect in BananaOS's Settings > Network.
